  "solution": {
    "text": "<h2>&nbsp;</h2><p>Polarization of EM Wave means Direction of Its electric Field</p><p>Electric field vector is along&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>So, unit electric filed vector,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;(Given)</p><p>Direction of wave,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>&nbsp; (Given)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;denotes unit magnetic field vector.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>General Form is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is Magnitude of Magnetic Field</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
